Rewrite the following Java 8 code into exactly 5 different variants. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Each variant should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input. Make the variants meaningfully different from one another and from the original code, while preserving functionality exactly.
Print all 5 rewritten variants, numbered from 1 to 5. Do not stop early, do not skip an index, and do not repeat an index. Use this exact format:
<perturbed_code_1>
<your_rewritten_code_1>
</perturbed_code_1>
<perturbed_code_2>
<your_rewritten_code_2>
</perturbed_code_2>
<perturbed_code_3>
<your_rewritten_code_3>
</perturbed_code_3>
<perturbed_code_4>
<your_rewritten_code_4>
</perturbed_code_4>
<perturbed_code_5>
<your_rewritten_code_5>
</perturbed_code_5>
Each block must contain one complete program. Do not provide any other text or markdown fences.

Here is the original Java 8 code you have to rewrite:
<original_code>
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);
        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);
        Solver s = new Solver();
        s.solve(in, out);
        out.close();
    }
    static class Solver {
        public void solve(Scanner in, PrintWriter out) {
            int n = in.nextInt();
            String s = in.next();
            int winpars = 0, longest = 0;
            int i = 0, j = 0;
            while (s.contains("__"))
                s = s.replaceAll("__", "_");
            n = s.length();
            if (s.charAt(i) == '(') {
                while (j < n && s.charAt(j++) != ')')
                if (s.charAt(j) == ')') {
                    String temp = s.substring(i + 1, j);
                    if (!temp.contains("_") && temp.length() > 0)
                        ++winpars;
                    else {
                        StringTokenizer tok = new StringTokenizer(temp, "_");
                        winpars += tok.countTokens();
                    }
                    i = j;
                }
            }
            while (i < n && s.charAt(i) != '(') {
                ++i;
                if (i < n && s.charAt(i) == '(') {
                    j = i;
                    while (j < n && s.charAt(j++) != ')')
                    if (s.charAt(j) == ')') {
                        String temp = s.substring(i + 1, j);
                        if (!temp.contains("_") && temp.length() > 0)
                            ++winpars;
                        else {
                            StringTokenizer tok = new StringTokenizer(temp, "_");
                            winpars += tok.countTokens();
                        }
                        i = j;
                    }
                }
            }
            while (s.indexOf('(') != -1 || s.indexOf(')') != -1)
                s = s.replaceAll("\\([^\\(]*\\)", "_");
            StringTokenizer tok = new StringTokenizer(s, "_");
            while (tok.hasMoreElements()) {
                String temp = tok.nextToken();
                if (temp.length() > longest)
                    longest = temp.length();
            }
            out.println(longest + " " + winpars);
        }
    }
}
